ab89ac46-06e3-42e3-90e7-bcdbf1233564	\N	The Big Idea	1	\N	\r\n# 🎯 The Big Idea\r\n\r\nLearning Dutch is not about filling your brain with disconnected words.\r\n\r\nIt is about discovering how the language works.\r\n\r\nFirst, recognize the pieces. Then discover the connections. Next, understand the patterns. Finally, use those patterns yourself.\r\n\r\nUnderstand → Connect → Practice → Master\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🌍 01 What Is Dutch?\r\n\r\nDutch is spoken primarily in the Netherlands and Belgium.\r\n\r\nDutch belongs to the Germanic language family, alongside English, German, Swedish, Norwegian, and Danish.\r\n\r\nThese languages are related, but they are not the same.\r\n\r\nThink of a family. Family members may share similarities, but each person is different.\r\n\r\nLanguages work in a similar way. Dutch has its own vocabulary, pronunciation, spelling and grammar.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔗 02 Dutch and English\r\n\r\n| 🇬🇧 English | 🇳🇱 Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| water | water |\r\n| book | boek |\r\n| house | huis |\r\n\r\nBecause Dutch and English are historically related, your English knowledge can help you recognize connections.\r\n\r\nWhen you discover a new Dutch word, ask yourself:\r\n\r\n> "Does this remind me of something I already know?"\r\n\r\nUse similarities as clues, not guarantees.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 03 A Language Is a System\r\n\r\nImagine building something with LEGO.\r\n\r\nOne piece is useful, but connecting several pieces lets you build something bigger.\r\n\r\nLanguage works similarly.\r\n\r\nWORDS → SENTENCES → MEANING\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Ik | I |\r\n| lees | read |\r\n| een boek | a book |\r\n\r\n**Ik lees een boek.**\r\n\r\nEnglish: *I read a book.*\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🗝️ 04 Your First Sentence Pattern\r\n\r\nIk\r\n↓\r\nperson\r\n\r\nlees\r\n↓\r\naction\r\n\r\neen boek\r\n↓\r\nthing\r\n\r\nPERSON → ACTION → THING\r\n\r\nEnglish: I → read → a book\r\n\r\nDutch: Ik → lees → een boek\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎉 Side Quest Complete\r\n\r\nTest your understanding before moving on.\r\n  	2026-10-14 10:52:51.044323+00	2609560f-4eee-4ec9-831e-5345191936ec	f	80
aa0481f7-84c6-44d7-a3cd-2175d739749b	\N	The Cognate Vault — Words You Already Own	2	\N	\r\n# 🎁 The Cognate Vault\r\n\r\nEnglish and Dutch are cousins. They grew up in the same house.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🔑 01 What Is a Cognate?\r\n\r\nA cognate is a word that exists in two languages because both inherited it from the same ancestor.\r\n\r\nBoth descend from **West Germanic**, so thousands of everyday words are shared.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧱 02 Identical Words\r\n\r\n| 🇬🇧 English | 🇳🇱 Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| hand | hand |\r\n| arm | arm |\r\n| lip | lip |\r\n| bed | bed |\r\n| lamp | lamp |\r\n| bank | bank |\r\n| water | water |\r\n| radio | radio |\r\n| computer | computer |\r\n| pen | pen |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Your First Frame\r\n\r\nIk → heb → een → [object]\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Ik | I |\r\n| heb | have |\r\n| een | a / an |\r\n\r\n- Ik heb een hand.\r\n- Ik heb een lamp.\r\n- Ik heb een bed.\r\n- Ik heb een pen.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 💡 04 Meridian Insight\r\n\r\n> Recognition beats memorization.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎉 Side Quest Complete\r\n  	2026-10-14 10:52:51.044323+00	2609560f-4eee-4ec9-831e-5345191936ec	f	80
