fc175e9b-4ca7-4121-b23c-4b25a290798b	\N	Adjectives Before Nouns — The Basic Rule	1	\N	\r\n# 🎨 Adjectives Before Nouns\r\n\r\nDutch adjectives sit before the noun. Just like English.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Basic Pattern\r\n\r\n> adjective → noun\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| een **groot** huis | a big house |\r\n| een **klein** kind | a small child |\r\n| een **mooi** meisje | a pretty girl |\r\n| een **oud** boek | an old book |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Common Adjectives\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English | Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| groot | big | klein | small |\r\n| mooi | beautiful | lelijk | ugly |\r\n| oud | old | nieuw | new |\r\n| goed | good | slecht | bad |\r\n| warm | warm | koud | cold |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Sentences\r\n\r\n- Ik heb een groot huis.\r\n- Hij heeft een klein kind.\r\n- Wij zien een mooi meisje.\r\n- Dat is een oud boek.\r\n- Zij woont in een nieuw appartement.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Adjective BEFORE noun. "een groot huis" not "een huis groot." Same as English.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎯 Done\r\n  	2026-10-14 11:43:42.99057+00	64361e46-f36d-411b-b78b-df3d202c0dc4	f	80
39aeee22-0d2f-4aee-892a-e0b80216a9e6	\N	The -E Ending — When It Changes	2	\N	\r\n# 🧩 The -E Ending — When It Changes\r\n\r\nAdjectives change form depending on what follows.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 Two Forms\r\n\r\n> **Base form** (no -e) → after **een** with a **het**-word\r\n>\r\n> **-e form** → everywhere else\r\n\r\n| Context | Form | Example |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| een + het-word | no -e | een **groot** huis |\r\n| de-word | -e | de **grote** man |\r\n| het-word with "het" | -e | het **grote** huis |\r\n| plural | -e | **grote** huizen |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 Why This Rule Exists\r\n\r\n- **een groot huis** — indefinite + neuter\r\n- **het grote huis** — definite + neuter\r\n\r\nThe `-e` marks definiteness. Same reason English changes "a" to "the".\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Examples\r\n\r\n- een **groot** huis (indef. het-word, no -e)\r\n- het **grote** huis (def. het-word, -e)\r\n- de **grote** man (de-word, -e)\r\n- een **grote** man (de-word, -e)\r\n- **grote** huizen (plural, -e)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Safe Habit\r\n\r\n> When in doubt, add -e.\r\n\r\n90% of the time, -e is correct. The exception is: **een** + **het-word**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Adjective takes -E everywhere EXCEPT after "een" with a HET-word. "een groot huis" (no -e) vs "het grote huis" (-e).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎯 Done\r\n  	2026-10-14 11:43:42.99057+00	64361e46-f36d-411b-b78b-df3d202c0dc4	f	80
0e866425-da05-461c-8157-5bb569661ed1	\N	Predicate Adjectives — After the Verb	3	\N	\r\n# 🎯 Predicate Adjectives — After the Verb\r\n\r\nWhen the adjective comes AFTER the verb (as a predicate), it never takes -e.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Rule\r\n\r\n> Adjective AFTER "is" / "wordt" / "blijft" → **no -e**.\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Het huis is **groot**. | The house is big. |\r\n| De man is **oud**. | The man is old. |\r\n| Het meisje is **mooi**. | The girl is beautiful. |\r\n\r\nNever:\r\n- ~~Het huis is grote.~~ ❌\r\n- ~~De man is oude.~~ ❌\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 Before vs After\r\n\r\n| Position | Form | Example |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Before noun | -e (mostly) | de **grote** man |\r\n| After verb | no -e | de man is **groot** |\r\n\r\nSame adjective. Two positions. Two forms.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 More Examples\r\n\r\n- De auto is **nieuw**.\r\n- Het boek is **oud**.\r\n- De koffie is **warm**.\r\n- Het water is **koud**.\r\n- Wij zijn **moe**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Common Predicate Adjectives\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| moe | tired |\r\n| blij | happy |\r\n| verdrietig | sad |\r\n| boos | angry |\r\n| ziek | sick |\r\n\r\n- Ik ben **moe**.\r\n- Jij bent **blij**.\r\n- Hij is **ziek**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Predicate adjective (after "is") NEVER takes -E. "Het huis is groot" not "grote." The -e only appears BEFORE the noun.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎯 Done\r\n  	2026-10-14 11:43:42.99057+00	64361e46-f36d-411b-b78b-df3d202c0dc4	f	80
907ad4ce-9e3a-4e7c-b44f-d25217d2573e	\N	Comparatives & Superlatives	4	\N	\r\n# 📊 Comparatives & Superlatives\r\n\r\nBigger. Biggest. Faster. Fastest.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Pattern\r\n\r\n> Comparative: adjective + **-er**\r\n>\r\n> Superlative: adjective + **-st**\r\n\r\n| Dutch | Comparative | Superlative |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| groot | groter | grootst |\r\n| klein | kleiner | kleinst |\r\n| mooi | mooier | mooist |\r\n| oud | ouder | oudst |\r\n| nieuw | nieuwer | nieuwst |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 The "dan" Connection\r\n\r\n> Comparative + **dan** = "than"\r\n\r\n- Hij is **groter dan** ik. (He is taller than me.)\r\n- Amsterdam is **kleiner dan** Londen.\r\n- Dit boek is **beter dan** dat boek.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Superlatives\r\n\r\n> **de / het** + adjective + **-st**\r\n\r\n- De grootste stad van Nederland.\r\n- Het mooiste huis in de straat.\r\n- De oudste man van het dorp.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Irregular Forms\r\n\r\n| Dutch | Comparative | Superlative | English |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| goed | beter | best | good |\r\n| veel | meer | meest | much / many |\r\n| weinig | minder | minst | little / few |\r\n\r\n- **goed** → **beter** → **best**\r\n- **veel** → **meer** → **meest**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Comparative = -ER + "dan". Superlative = -ST. Irregulars: goed → beter → best. veel → meer → meest.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎯 Done\r\n  	2026-10-14 11:43:42.99057+00	64361e46-f36d-411b-b78b-df3d202c0dc4	f	80
