6f7bb638-fbf1-4aa0-bf09-cb54b8726d21	\N	Mission 2 Recap — Everything You Built	1	\N	\r\n# 🎯 Mission 2 Recap — Everything You Built\r\n\r\nFour sagas. One leap. You are no longer a beginner.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧱 01 What You Own\r\n\r\n| Area | Content |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Regular verbs | stem + endings (ik / jij / hij / wij) |\r\n| Word order | V2 — verb in position 2 |\r\n| Inversion | front → invert |\r\n| Adverbs | time → manner → place |\r\n| Questions | verb-first, QW-first |\r\n| Negation | geen + niet |\r\n| Adjectives | before-noun -e, predicate no -e |\r\n| Comparatives | -er + dan, -st |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📚 02 The Verb Engine\r\n\r\n| Pronoun | Ending |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ik | stem |\r\n| jij / u / hij / zij / het | stem + t |\r\n| wij / jullie / zij | stem + en |\r\n\r\nThree unique forms per verb. Always.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 The Sentence Shapes\r\n\r\n| Shape | Position 1 | Position 2 | Position 3 |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Statement | Subject | Verb | Rest |\r\n| Fronted | Topic | Verb | Subject |\r\n| Yes/no Q | Verb | Subject | Rest |\r\n| QW Q | QW | Verb | Subject |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Negation\r\n\r\n| Word | Position |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| geen | before indefinite noun |\r\n| niet | end of sentence (default) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 05 Adjectives\r\n\r\n| Position | Form |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Before noun | -e, EXCEPT een + het-word |\r\n| After "is" | no -e |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Mission 2 gave you: verb engine, V2 word order, question formation, negation, adjectives. These five pillars support every Dutch sentence you will ever build.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 🎯 Done\r\n\r\nNext: the Mission 2 Exam. 40 questions. 80% to pass.\r\n  	2026-10-14 11:44:10.196639+00	cffce8fe-386f-40a6-9300-c44930140a0f	f	80
