ebf57736-ba7a-4a7c-870d-25952e7abf8a	\N	Numbers 1–20 — The Foundation	1	\N	\r\n# 🔢 Numbers 1–20 — The Foundation\r\n\r\nEvery conversation uses numbers. Here is the complete set.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Table\r\n\r\n| # | Dutch | # | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | een | 11 | elf |\r\n| 2 | twee | 12 | twaalf |\r\n| 3 | drie | 13 | dertien |\r\n| 4 | vier | 14 | veertien |\r\n| 5 | vijf | 15 | vijftien |\r\n| 6 | zes | 16 | zestien |\r\n| 7 | zeven | 17 | zeventien |\r\n| 8 | acht | 18 | achttien |\r\n| 9 | negen | 19 | negentien |\r\n| 10 | tien | 20 | twintig |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 The Pattern (13–19)\r\n\r\n> Number + **-tien** (ten)\r\n\r\n- **drie** → **dertien** (3 → 13)\r\n- **vier** → **veertien** (4 → 14)\r\n- **vijf** → **vijftien** (5 → 15)\r\n\r\nSame as English: "thir-teen", "four-teen".\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Common Uses\r\n\r\n- Ik ben **twintig** jaar. (I am 20 years old.)\r\n- Ik heb **twee** broers.\r\n- Dat kost **vijf** euro.\r\n- Het is **drie** uur.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 💡 04 Meridian Insight\r\n\r\n> 1-20 is the core. Master these, everything else is pattern.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Numbers 1–10 are unique (memorize them). 11–12 are irregular (elf, twaalf). 13–19 = base number + "-TIEN". 20 = twintig.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
d0ce25cb-1316-424f-84a7-97edc8767d55	\N	Numbers 20–100 — The Scale	2	\N	\r\n# 📊 Numbers 20–100 — The Scale\r\n\r\nOnce you know 1–20, the rest is pattern.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Tens\r\n\r\n| # | Dutch | # | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 20 | twintig | 60 | zestig |\r\n| 30 | dertig | 70 | zeventig |\r\n| 40 | veertig | 80 | tachtig |\r\n| 50 | vijftig | 90 | negentig |\r\n| 100 | honderd | | |\r\n\r\nNotice: **-tig** ending (like English "-ty").\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 The 21–99 Formula\r\n\r\n> **unit + en + ten**\r\n\r\nYes — Dutch says **"one and twenty"** not "twenty-one".\r\n\r\n| # | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 21 | eenentwintig (one-and-twenty) |\r\n| 22 | tweeëntwintig |\r\n| 35 | vijfendertig |\r\n| 47 | zevenenveertig |\r\n| 99 | negenennegentig |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Hundreds\r\n\r\n- 100 = honderd\r\n- 200 = tweehonderd\r\n- 500 = vijfhonderd\r\n- 999 = negenhonderdnegenennegentig\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Examples\r\n\r\n- Ik woon op **nummer twaalf**.\r\n- Het kost **vijfentwintig** euro.\r\n- Wij hebben **honderd** boeken.\r\n- Dat is **negenennegentig** procent.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: 21+ = UNIT + EN + TEN. Dutch says "eenentwintig" (one-and-twenty) not "twenty-one". Same shape as old English.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
afcddd7b-bbd2-425a-9aed-bd8f5cf661d9	\N	Days of the Week	3	\N	\r\n# 📅 Days of the Week\r\n\r\nSeven days. Notice how similar they are to English.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Days\r\n\r\n| English | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Monday | maandag |\r\n| Tuesday | dinsdag |\r\n| Wednesday | woensdag |\r\n| Thursday | donderdag |\r\n| Friday | vrijdag |\r\n| Saturday | zaterdag |\r\n| Sunday | zondag |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🧠 02 The Pattern\r\n\r\n> Almost every day ends in **-dag** (day).\r\n\r\n- **maan**dag = moon day\r\n- **dins**dag (named after Tyr)\r\n- **woens**dag (Woden's day)\r\n- **donder**dag = thunder day\r\n- **vrij**dag = free day\r\n- **zater**dag = Saturn's day\r\n- **zon**dag = sun day\r\n\r\nSame etymological roots as English!\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Sentences\r\n\r\n- **Vandaag** is het maandag. (Today is Monday.)\r\n- **Morgen** is het dinsdag.\r\n- Ik werk op **vrijdag**.\r\n- Wij gaan op **zondag** naar de kerk.\r\n- Op **woensdag** heb ik tijd.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Days & Prepositions\r\n\r\n| Preposition | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| op maandag | on Monday |\r\n| elke maandag | every Monday |\r\n| deze maandag | this Monday |\r\n| volgende maandag | next Monday |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: All days end in "-DAG". "op" + day for "on [day]". Days are NOT capitalized in Dutch (unlike English).\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
93841474-01c4-42a4-8bb1-0e6a84103611	\N	Months & Seasons	4	\N	\r\n# 🌍 Months & Seasons\r\n\r\nTwelve months. Four seasons. Both follow recognizable patterns.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Months\r\n\r\n| English | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| January | januari |\r\n| February | februari |\r\n| March | maart |\r\n| April | april |\r\n| May | mei |\r\n| June | juni |\r\n| July | juli |\r\n| August | augustus |\r\n| September | september |\r\n| October | oktober |\r\n| November | november |\r\n| December | december |\r\n\r\nNearly identical to English. Latin roots.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 The Seasons\r\n\r\n| English | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| spring | lente / voorjaar |\r\n| summer | zomer |\r\n| autumn | herfst / najaar |\r\n| winter | winter |\r\n\r\n> Both **lente** and **voorjaar** mean spring. Both **herfst** and **najaar** mean autumn. Regional preference.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 In Sentences\r\n\r\n- **In januari** is het koud. (In January it is cold.)\r\n- **In de zomer** gaan wij naar zee.\r\n- Mijn verjaardag is **in mei**.\r\n- **In de herfst** vallen de bladeren.\r\n- **In de winter** sneeuwt het.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Month Preposition\r\n\r\n> **in** + month\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| in januari | in January |\r\n| in maart | in March |\r\n| in december | in December |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Months are NOT capitalized in Dutch. Use "IN" + month. "In januari", "in mei". Seasons also lowercase: "in de zomer".\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
c7ac475e-1c46-4cf0-82fc-32cb4625f010	\N	Review — Numbers, Days, Months (SQ 1–4)	5	\N	\r\n# 🔄 Review — Numbers, Days, Months\r\n\r\nFour lessons. Consolidate the calendar.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📚 01 Number Scale\r\n\r\n| Range | Rule |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 1–10 | unique |\r\n| 11–12 | irregular (elf, twaalf) |\r\n| 13–19 | base + -tien |\r\n| 20–90 | base + -tig |\r\n| 21–99 | unit + en + ten |\r\n| 100+ | honderd + unit |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Days\r\n\r\nmaandag · dinsdag · woensdag · donderdag · vrijdag · zaterdag · zondag\r\n\r\nAll end in -dag.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Months\r\n\r\njanuari · februari · maart · april · mei · juni · juli · augustus · september · oktober · november · december\r\n\r\nNearly identical to English.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Practice\r\n\r\nRead aloud:\r\n\r\n- Ik ben twintig jaar.\r\n- Vandaag is het maandag.\r\n- In januari is het koud.\r\n- Dat kost vijfenveertig euro.\r\n- Op zaterdag werk ik niet.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Numbers, days, months. All three systems share recognizable patterns with English. Learn the pattern, not the list.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
0377c3e9-f915-4a02-86a1-9a7aa3bc9373	\N	Telling Time — Hoe laat is het?	6	\N	\r\n# 🕐 Telling Time — Hoe laat is het?\r\n\r\nThe most useful question: "What time is it?"\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Question\r\n\r\n> **Hoe laat is het?** (What time is it?)\r\n>\r\n> **Het is ___ uur.** (It is ___ o'clock.)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Hours\r\n\r\n| Time | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 1:00 | Het is één uur. |\r\n| 2:00 | Het is twee uur. |\r\n| 5:00 | Het is vijf uur. |\r\n| 12:00 | Het is twaalf uur. |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Minutes\r\n\r\n| Time | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 5:10 | tien over vijf |\r\n| 5:15 | kwart over vijf |\r\n| 5:30 | half zes |\r\n| 5:40 | twintig voor zes |\r\n| 5:45 | kwart voor zes |\r\n\r\n> ⚠️ **half zes** = 5:30, NOT 6:30! Dutch "half" means "half-way to the next hour."\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Real Phrases\r\n\r\n- **Hoe laat is het?** — What time is it?\r\n- **Het is half drie.** — It is 2:30.\r\n- **Het is kwart voor acht.** — It is 7:45.\r\n- **Ik kom om drie uur.** — I come at 3 o'clock.\r\n- **Wij eten om half zeven.** — We eat at 6:30.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: "HALF DRIE" = 2:30, not 3:30. Dutch "half" points to the NEXT hour. Also: "kwart over" = quarter past, "kwart voor" = quarter to.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
04634cf0-5cde-4e78-bcf8-f9bbee661c82	\N	Dates & Years	7	\N	\r\n# 📆 Dates & Years\r\n\r\nHow to say dates, years, and birthdays.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 The Question\r\n\r\n> **Wat is de datum?** (What is the date?)\r\n>\r\n> **De datum is ___.**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Dates\r\n\r\n> **[day] + [month]**\r\n\r\n| Date | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| January 1 | één januari |\r\n| March 15 | vijftien maart |\r\n| May 20 | twintig mei |\r\n| December 31 | eenendertig december |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Years\r\n\r\n> Years are said as full numbers:\r\n\r\n| Year | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 1990 | negentienhonderd negentig |\r\n| 2000 | tweeduizend |\r\n| 2024 | tweeduizend vierentwintig |\r\n| 2025 | tweeduizend vijfentwintig |\r\n\r\n> Alternative: **negentien-negentig** (19-90) — both are common.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Birthdays\r\n\r\n- **Mijn verjaardag is op 15 maart.** — My birthday is on March 15.\r\n- **Wanneer is jouw verjaardag?** — When is your birthday?\r\n- **Ik ben geboren in 1995.** — I was born in 1995.\r\n\r\nNew verb: **geboren** (born) — used with "ben".\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 05 Ordinal Numbers\r\n\r\n| # | English | Dutch |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 1st | first | eerste |\r\n| 2nd | second | tweede |\r\n| 3rd | third | derde |\r\n| 4th | fourth | vierde |\r\n| 5th | fifth | vijfde |\r\n\r\n> Numbers 1–19 → +**-de**. 20+ → +**-ste**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Dates = "day month" (no "of"). Years split in half: "1990" = "negentienhonderd negentig". Ordinal: 1st–19th = +"-de", 20th+ = +"-ste".\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
d1dad859-7b90-42e9-a432-d97eaa481c3e	\N	Time Expressions — Always, Often, Sometimes	8	\N	\r\n# ⏳ Time Expressions — Frequency & Duration\r\n\r\nTen time words that multiply your sentences by ten.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 Frequency\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| altijd | always |\r\n| vaak | often |\r\n| soms | sometimes |\r\n| nooit | never |\r\n| zelden | rarely |\r\n| meestal | usually |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Duration\r\n\r\n| Dutch | English |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| lang | long |\r\n| kort | short |\r\n| even | briefly / a moment |\r\n| de hele dag | all day |\r\n| elke dag | every day |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 In Sentences\r\n\r\n- Ik drink **altijd** koffie in de ochtend.\r\n- Wij gaan **vaak** naar de markt.\r\n- Hij werkt **soms** thuis.\r\n- Zij komt **nooit** te laat.\r\n- Ik lees **elke dag** een boek.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Position\r\n\r\nTime expressions **front** the sentence OR **follow the verb**:\r\n\r\n| Sentence | Position |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Altijd** drink ik koffie. | front (with inversion) |\r\n| Ik drink **altijd** koffie. | after verb |\r\n| **Vaak** gaan wij naar de markt. | front |\r\n| Wij gaan **vaak** naar de markt. | after verb |\r\n\r\nBoth work. Fronting adds emphasis.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Frequency words can go in position 1 (with inversion) OR after the verb. "Altijd drink ik koffie" = "Ik drink altijd koffie". Both correct.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
76d14141-b542-4b66-bea8-a985c48c7a87	\N	Reading Practice — Time in Real Sentences	9	\N	\r\n# 📖 Reading Practice — Time in Real Sentences\r\n\r\nNumbers, days, months, time. All together.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 01 Simple\r\n\r\n1. Het is drie uur.\r\n2. Vandaag is het maandag.\r\n3. Ik ben twintig jaar oud.\r\n4. Mijn verjaardag is in mei.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 02 Medium\r\n\r\n5. Wij gaan elke zaterdag naar de markt.\r\n6. Ik drink altijd koffie om acht uur.\r\n7. In de zomer is het warm in Nederland.\r\n8. Op vrijdag werk ik tot vijf uur.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 03 Longer\r\n\r\n9. Mijn vader is geboren op 15 maart 1965.\r\n10. Wij eten meestal om half zeven.\r\n11. In december is het koud en donker.\r\n12. Elke ochtend loop ik een half uur.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🎯 04 Find the Time Word\r\n\r\nIdentify the time expression in each sentence:\r\n\r\n- *Ik drink altijd koffie.* → altijd\r\n- *Op vrijdag werk ik.* → op vrijdag\r\n- *In de zomer is het warm.* → in de zomer\r\n- *Wij eten om half zeven.* → om half zeven\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Real Dutch sentences LOVE time words. Nearly every natural sentence has a "when". Practice placing them in position 1 or after the verb.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:00:44.031471+00	303a01fd-7d00-4dd3-9b50-78fe73b41e16	f	80
