de2d1c17-4eb8-4b29-8fe2-668684909c07	\N	Mission 4 Recap — Connected Thinker	1	\N	\r\n# 🎯 Mission 4 Recap — Connected Thinker\r\n\r\nYou went from isolated sentences to flowing paragraphs.\r\n\r\n## What You Own\r\n\r\n| Area | Content |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Coordinating conjunctions | en, maar, of, want, dus |\r\n| Subordinating conjunctions | omdat, als, terwijl, hoewel, dat, of |\r\n| Past tense | Perfectum + Imperfectum |\r\n| Subordinate clauses | Verb-to-END rule |\r\n| Relative clauses | die / dat / waar / wie |\r\n| Indirect speech | dat + subclause |\r\n| Separable verbs | Splits in main, stays in sub |\r\n| Future | Gaan + zullen + zou |\r\n\r\n## The Three Word-Order Rules\r\n\r\n1. **Main clause**: verb in position 2\r\n2. **Subclause**: verb at END\r\n3. **Front + invert**: anything front → verb before subject\r\n\r\n## The Past Tenses\r\n\r\n| Tense | When | Example |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Perfectum | Spoken | Ik heb gewerkt. |\r\n| Imperfectum | Written | Ik werkte. |\r\n\r\n## The Future\r\n\r\n| Form | Use |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| gaan + inf | casual plans |\r\n| zullen + inf | promises / predictions |\r\n| zou + inf | polite / hypothetical |\r\n\r\n## Full sentence example\r\n\r\n**Als ik morgen tijd heb, dan ga ik je opbellen, omdat ik je iets belangrijks moet vertellen.**\r\n\r\n- Sub 1: Als ik morgen tijd **heb**\r\n- Main inverted: **ga ik** je opbellen\r\n- Sub 2: omdat ik je iets belangrijks moet **vertellen**\r\n\r\n> ✍️ WRITE THIS DOWN: Mission 4 = the tools to link thoughts. Coordinating + Subordinating + Past + Future + Separable. You can now build paragraphs.\r\n  	2026-10-14 12:39:27.685464+00	a4a3a321-8d3f-462d-8ffd-1c66441fadee	f	80
